From a8a20aeb665de58bcd3a3e35233fb62a1e9214f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:55:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): the same-second checkpoint and cooldown readers
 skip unused Board grants [daveey]

Two respawn-guard readers still took the newest ended run row, so a Board
grant returned unused (outcome 'released', metadata {"unused_grant": true})
counted as the card's latest run:

- _immediate_checkpoint_after (same-second kanban_continue handoff) skipped
  core-update requeues but not grants: one release_unused after claim, PR
  comment and continue in one second held the owner active_pr.
- check_respawn_guard's cooldown reader (ORDER BY ended_at DESC LIMIT 1)
  skipped neither: a grant ending after an infrastructure spawn_failed or an
  owner-restart run ended infrastructure_cooldown / owner_restart_cooldown
  early.

Both now use latest_ended_run_skipping_requeues, the ended-run variant of
the picker the other review-continuation readers use (the cooldown reader
keeps its ended_at ordering). Any run that started, failed or lacks the
unused-grant receipt still counts. latest_run_skipping_requeues loses its
skip_unused_grants keyword (no caller passed False).

Tests: RED on main for both readers; added coverage for a replica card
(run_uid park identity, remapped run ids), a picker with only grants
(None), and hold release() refusing "already used for this park" across
a grant. release_unused (test helper) now also clears claim_expires.
